<title>AUSTRALIA: St George ups job loss estimate to 1,400.</title>
<headline>St George ups job loss estimate to 1,400.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>St George Bank Ltd said on Tuesday that it had revised its estimate of job reductions following its takeover of Advance Bank Ltd to 1,400 workers from 1,000 previously.  </p>
<p>The losses are expected to occur over a 30 month period.</p>
<p>&quot;One hundred people have already gone,&quot; managing director Jim Sweeney told reporters.</p>
<p>&quot;But the actual number of people that will be leaving the bank will number only about 800,&quot; Sweeney said, explaining that the other losses reflected natural attrition from the bank.</p>
<p>St George completed its A$2.635 billion takeover of Advance Bank earlier in calendar 1997. The latter bank contributed A$19.1 million to the combined group's first half net profit of A$99.7 million to March 31. This compared with A$74.5 million a year ago. -- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
